CLOSE(2)                       P32W Unix                        CLOSE(2)

NAME
       close - close a file descriptor

SYNOPSIS
       #include <unistd.h>

       int close(int fd);

DESCRIPTION
       close frees the file descriptor fd. When the last descriptor
       referring to an open file goes (descriptors are shared by
       dup(2) and fork(2)), the file is closed: for a pipe the
       other end then sees end of file or gets SIGPIPE; for a
       device its driver's close routine runs; for a block device
       the buffer cache is written out; a file that has been
       unlinked is freed when nothing has it open any more.

       Every open descriptor is closed when a process exits.

RETURN VALUE
       0 on success; -1 on an error, with errno set.

ERRORS
       EBADF   fd is not an open file descriptor.

SEE ALSO
       open(2), pipe(2), dup(2), exit(2)
